"""Explore how big the Ubuntu archive is, and how much of it is kernels.

Reads binary and source indexes straight from the Ubuntu snapshot service, so
it can look at any point in time since 2023-03-01 rather than just whatever
apt happens to have locally.  Everything it downloads is reduced and cached, so
the expensive first run is the only expensive run.

  archive-size-explorer build -o archive.html     # fetch + write the page
  archive-size-explorer report -s noble           # text summary of one snapshot
  archive-size-explorer breakdown --family        # where the space actually goes
  archive-size-explorer cache                     # what the cache is holding

The output of "build" is a single self-contained HTML file: open it with
file://, no server needed.
"""

